Modifications
-------------

The Muninn fork began in 2026, based on the Linkwarden baseline noted above.
Relative to that baseline, the modifications include the following. This section
is provided to satisfy AGPL-3.0 section 5(a), which requires a modified work to
carry prominent notices stating that it was changed and giving a relevant date.

  - Added a board/dashboard layer (Board, Section, BoardItem, BoardMember data
    models) on top of the existing owner-scoped Collection/Link model, providing
    a Homarr-style tile dashboard while inheriting the per-user data-isolation
    and granular member-permission (create/update/delete) model.
  - Added complete versioned REST API coverage for every board and layout
    mutation (boards, sections, items, single and bulk item repositioning, board
    members, widget-type registry) so a client can manage layout end to end
    without any browser interaction.
  - Added a server-side widget framework and a set of pluggable, configuration-
    driven widget integrations (torrent queue, media-request list, indexer
    health, an arbitrary-PromQL stat tile, ping/uptime, and calendar). Widget
    endpoints and credentials are supplied per item at runtime; none are
    hardcoded.
  - Fixed the admin-user-provisioning defect (upstream issue #984) so that
    disabling public self-registration no longer disables administrator-initiated
    user creation; introduced a real instance-level admin role and centralized
    the admin-authorization check.
  - Added a tamper-evident, append-only, hash-chained administrative audit log.
  - Rebranded the user interface and application identity from the upstream
    project to Muninn, with a dark "Cobalt" theme.

Relevant date: fork initiated 2026; see https://github.com/Emkraan/muninn for
the complete revision history.


